    "abstract": null,
    "field": "Elevation-dependent warming",
    "problem": "Accurately quantifying elevation-dependent warming is challenging due to sparse high-elevation observations, extreme local climate variability, and the limitations of satellite data and climate models.",
    "method": "The paper proposes a strategy that combines an enhanced network of field observations, satellite remote sensing, and high-resolution climate modeling to increase knowledge of elevation-dependent warming trends and their controlling mechanisms.",
    "task": "The task is to review the evidence and mechanisms for elevation-dependent warming (EDW) in mountain regions, and to discuss future research needs including improved observations, remote sensing, and modeling to better understand the phenomenon.",
